\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The bounds stay inside the finite inequality}
\date{2026-11-21}

\p{The determinant identity is the rank-one formula of
\ref{fdip-013I}. The lower bound is the inequality of
\ref{fdip-0134} on one basis vector. Neither step uses the
maximization of a quotient on the compact sphere.
\ref{fdip-011Y} records that maximization as the source of
the Rayleigh hypothesis. \ref{fdip-013I} gives one
characteristic polynomial to a matrix and to its rescaling,
and \ref{fdip-0136} applies that identity on this edge.}
